"claim_text": "Hi,\nI’m reporting a crash from yesterday (September 15th). I was driving my 2019 Subaru Outback (VIN98123746509283746, estimated value ~$17,350) when another car rear-ended me on the interstate. I wanted to mention I also own a Toyota Corolla (2017, VIN29384756109283744, ~$11,200), which is under the same policy POL-119384756, but that car was parked at home and not involved. Please don’t mix them up.\nThe highway patrol officer filed report PR-20250915-4419. The mechanic’s estimate came to $6,321 in damages for the Outback—mostly bumper and exhaust replacement.\n---\n[Attached PDF: Policy Printout]\n\nPolicy #: POL-119384756  \nHolder: Laura Adams  \nCoverage: Auto  \nEffective: 05-Nov-2023  \nExpires: 04-Nov-2025  \nInsured Vehicles: Subaru Outback 2019, Toyota Corolla 2017\n---\nThanks,  Laura\nI'm also thinking of including my 2020 Mazda CX-5, estimated at $20k, in the policy in the future, but I haven't gotten to that yet.\nRespond with a JSON object in the following order of fields: `claim` (must be formatted as a valid Python InsuranceClaim)." 

